SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when the engine refused to stop\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_create (uint32_t * buffer, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t stride, \fBschultz_thorvg\fP ** out_backend)"

.PP
Creates a backend that rasterizes into a caller owned buffer\&. The buffer is not copied and must stay valid and unmoved for the life of the backend\&. Pixels are written as premultiplied ARGB8888, which is what SDL's SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888 expects on a little endian machine\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbuffer\fP Destination pixels, at least stride * height words\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIwidth\fP Buffer width in pixels\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIheight\fP Buffer height in pixels\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIstride\fP Distance between rows, in pixels, not bytes\&. Must be at least width\&. 
.br
\fIout_backend\fP Receives the new backend\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a bad argument, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY when the canvas could not be created\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void schultz_thorvg_destroy (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend)"

.PP
Destroys a backend and its canvas\&. The pixel buffer belongs to the caller and is not freed\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to destroy\&. NULL is accepted and does nothing\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_set_target (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend, uint32_t * buffer, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t stride)"

.PP
Points the canvas at a different buffer\&. A window that has been resized has a new buffer of a new size, and the canvas has to be told or it keeps rasterizing into the old one\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to retarget\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIbuffer\fP The new destination pixels, owned by the caller\&. 
.br
\fIwidth\fP Its width in pixels\&. 
.br
\fIheight\fP Its height in pixels\&. 
.br
\fIstride\fP Pixels per row, not bytes\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_set_fonts (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend, \fBschultz_font_system\fP * system, \fBschultz_glyph_cache\fP * cache)"

.PP
Gives the backend what it needs to draw text\&. Until this is called, a glyph run command fails rather than drawing nothing, so missing text is reported instead of silently absent\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to configure\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIsystem\fP The font system glyph run commands name fonts in\&. Must not be NULL and must outlive the backend\&. 
.br
\fIcache\fP The glyph cache to rasterize through\&. Must not be NULL and must outlive the backend\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when any pointer is NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_painter (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend, \fBschultz_painter\fP * out_painter)"

.PP
Fills in a painter that draws through this backend\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to bind\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIout_painter\fP Receives the vtable and context\&. Must not be NULL\&. It borrows the backend, so the backend must outlive it\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when either pointer is NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_set_resources (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend, \fBschultz_resource_table\fP * table)"

.PP
Tells the backend where registered gradients and dashes live\&. A draw command names a gradient or a dash pattern by handle, and this is where the backend looks it up\&. Without a table, a gradient draws nothing and a dash pattern is ignored, which is what a caller using only solid colours wants\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to configure\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItable\fP The table, or NULL to remove it\&. Not owned, and must outlive the backend\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when backend is NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_set_scale (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend, float scale)"

.PP
Sets how many buffer pixels there are to a toolkit unit\&. One by default, which is a screen at its own resolution\&. Larger renders the same tree at higher resolution without laying it out again: a page at print resolution, or a thumbnail scaled the other way\&. Glyphs are rasterized at the scaled size rather than blown up from screen size, so text stays as sharp as everything around it\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to configure\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIscale\fP Buffer pixels per toolkit unit\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_thorvg_set_images (\fBschultz_thorvg\fP * backend, \fBschultz_image_table\fP * table)"

.PP
Tells the backend where loaded images live\&. A draw command names an image by handle, and this is where the backend looks it up\&. Without a table an image draws nothing, which is what a caller that never loads one wants\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbackend\fP The backend to configure\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItable\fP The table, or NULL to remove it\&. Not owned, and must outlive the backend\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when backend is NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

